# Python environments -- rebuilt from pyproject.toml/requirements.txt, never committed.
# .venv-linux/ in particular is ~5.3GB (a full standalone install, not
# --system-site-packages like .venv/) -- committing it would make every clone
# multi-gigabyte for no reason, since it's 100% regenerable from the pinned deps.
.venv/
.venv-linux/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/

# Trained model checkpoints (~1GB across all training stages) and TensorBoard event
# logs -- large, regenerable (via the training commands in README.md), and not needed
# to read/audit the results themselves (the CSVs/tables/figures are what's cited).
# The COMPLETE archive, including every checkpoint, ships as the Zenodo deposit
# (FINAL_REPRODUCIBILITY_REPORT.md Section 5) -- that is the canonical, full-
# reproduction artifact; this git repository is the code + small result-summary layer.
**/checkpoints/*.zip
**/tb_logs/
**/experiments/results/optuna_*.db

# OS/editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.Rhistory

